  Rule detail: replace only exact token `[[TARGET]]` (and `[[TARGET|alias]]` variants) with `[[NEW]]` (keep alias) for 改链; for 断链保文 replace `[[TARGET]]` → `TARGET` (strip brackets, keep text; for `[[TARGET|alias]]` → alias). For YAML related lines `- "[[TARGET]]"` where TARGET maps to strip → the line becomes `- "TARGET"` plain string, harmless. Or delete? If the YAML related entry maps to a real card → 改链. If strip → it becomes a plain text entry in related — that pollutes related with non-ids. Better: for pure list lines (frontmatter/list where the entire item is the link), DELETE the line when mapping=断链. For inline → strip brackets.

